--- TEST 4b: |G|^2 = 2^{v2} * (odd part). Clifford Gauss sum would have odd part = 1 ---
n=4: |G|^2=20 = 2^2 * 5   (full factorization {2: 2, 5: 1}); odd-part>1 => c3-mod-4 phase is NOT a pure GF(2) Gauss sum
n=5: |G|^2=544 = 2^5 * 17   (full factorization {2: 5, 17: 1}); odd-part>1 => c3-mod-4 phase is NOT a pure GF(2) Gauss sum
n=6: |G|^2=32000 = 2^8 * 125   (full factorization {2: 8, 5: 3}); odd-part>1 => c3-mod-4 phase is NOT a pure GF(2) Gauss sum
n=7: |G|^2=1675264 = 2^12 * 409   (full factorization {2: 12, 409: 1}); odd-part>1 => c3-mod-4 phase is NOT a pure GF(2) Gauss sum

