======================================================================
STATUS SUMMARY
======================================================================
PROVED  : c3 = C(n,3) - sum_v C(s_v,2) is an INTEGER QUADRATIC FORM in the F=C(n-1,2)
          tile bits (degree exactly 2: all 3rd mixed differences vanish; full 2^F match).
          => the c3 / score layer is the 'Clifford' (Gauss-sum/quadratic) tractable level.
VERIFIED: extracted (c0,L,Q) reproduces c3 bit-for-bit; reproduces THM-554 Z_n c3-dist;
          imaginary Gauss sum sum_b i^{c3(b)} computed two ways agree.
VERIFIED: H is EXACTLY quadratic (magic fraction 0) at n=4; magic (deg>=3 Fourier energy
          fraction) = 0, 0.299, 0.510, 0.635 at n=4,5,6,7 -- monotone rise = magic onset.
          max-degree(H) tracks the longest odd cycle (n=7 reaches degree 6 = c_7).
CONJECTURE: the deg>=3 Fourier energy of H is the tournament 'stabilizer-rank/magic'
          monotone; it is 0 exactly when H is a pure Gauss sum (n=4).
REFUTED : naive 'regular/Paley has more LOCAL magic (avg 3rd diff)' -- avg is LOWER for
          regular than transitive at every n tested. Local d3 is the WRONG monotone;
          the global degree>=3 Fourier energy is the right one.
ARITHMETIC: odd part of |G|^2 (5,17,125,409 at n=4..7) > 1 => the c3-mod-4 phase is a
          DEGENERATE/non-stabilizer Gauss sum -- a quantitative arithmetic magic signature.
